## Rows skipped

id-a 12 and id-b 9 — delete U+200B / join the zero-width blank lines (003 Q16–Q20, 005 including `**​**`, 006, 008, 009, 013, 015).
Reason: `checkBlocks` requires the target ZWSP count to equal the Korean source. Counts left as-is: 003=52, 005=8, 006=4, 008=10, 009=5, 013=5, 015=3 (87). Deleting them also changes the non-empty block count, because a ZWSP-only line is a block.

id-a 13 — turn Pertanyaan 16–20 into `##` headings.
Reason: Korean (and English) keep Q16–Q20 as plain lines while Q1–Q15 are headings. `checkHeadings` compares heading levels exactly. Adding headings would fail. Not a translation error.

id-b 6 — “Uraian di atas merupakan saran perancangan kontrak.”
Reason: the Korean source says “이상은 계약 설계 제안입니다” and the English says “The foregoing is contract-design advice.” The Indonesian matches both. Rewriting it as “hanya membandingkan jalur pendirian cabang dan anak perusahaan” would change the source proposition. Listed under reviewer disagreements.

id-b 13 — renumber `## 7` to `## 6`.
Reason: Korean and English use the same 5 → 7 → 8 skip. Renumbering only the Indonesian heading would diverge from the source. Heading levels already match, so the checker does not want a text renumber.

