## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)

1. Zero-width blanks are not an Indonesian writing choice. They are inherited from the Korean source and the checker locks the count. Joining them into ordinary paragraphs would fail `blocks` / `ZWSP`.
2. Q16–Q20 are body lines in the Korean and English files as well. Making only the Indonesian ones into headings would fail the heading-level check.
3. Section numbering 5, 7, 8 in column 018 is the same in Korean and English. It is not an Indonesian outline error.
4. “Saran perancangan kontrak” after the branch/subsidiary comparison is the Korean and English sentence, not a mistranslation of those paragraphs.
5. On the 004 link, the correct statute is the withholding-rate standard, Article 3, but the checker still requires the digit 10 from the Korean label “영업세법 제10조”. The published label names the right instrument and says it is not Business Tax Act Article 10, so the digit survives. The URL was not changed.
